## Your settings

Select your avatar at the bottom of the side bar, then **Settings**. The settings menu has:

| Page | Use |
|---|---|
| **Profile** | Your photo, name and contact details. The profile is kept by HR: to change anything on it, ask HR. |
| **Working status** | Tell colleagues whether you are available, and until when. |
| **Notifications** | For each kind of event, choose whether it is shown **In app**, sent by **Email**, or both. **Email notifications** turns all e-mails off or on. Password resets, invitations and system alerts are always sent. |
| **Language & region** | The interface language, time zone, time format, date format and first day of the week (below). |
| **Account security** | Passkey, authenticator app, recovery codes and password. See [Two-step verification and account security](/en/getting-started/account-security/). |
| **Sessions & devices** | The devices where you are signed in. Sign out one device, or select **Sign out all other devices**. **Sign-in history** lists recent sign-ins. |
| **Approval delegations** | Send the approvals addressed to you to a colleague between two dates, for example while you are on leave. Under **New delegation**, choose the colleague and the start and end dates, and select **Create delegation**; end one early with **Revoke**. |

## Language

Operon can be used in English or Chinese. Each user chooses their own language; a new account is in English.

{% steps %}
1. Open **Settings** › **Language & region**.
2. In **Language**, choose **English** or **中文**.
{% /steps %}

The choice is saved at once and the whole interface changes immediately; you do not need to sign in again. It follows your account to every computer you use.

The language does not change:

- **What the AI employees write.** They reply in the language of your message. Only when your message has no clear language (for example, only a UEN or "OK"), or when the employee writes first, do they use your interface language.
- **Documents and e-mails for clients and authorities** — for example reports, statutory documents and Operon's e-mails. These are in English.
- **Names entered in Operon**, such as company names, case titles and workflow names, which are shown as they were entered.

## Get help

| Where | What it gives you |
|---|---|
| **User manual** in the side bar | This manual, in a new tab, in your interface language. |
| **Contact support** in the side bar | Our support e-mail address. Select **Send email** to write to us from your e-mail program, or **Copy address**. |
| Your tenant admin | Accounts, roles, access to suites and companies, and resets of passwords and two-step verification. |

When you write to support, say what you were trying to do, what you selected, and what happened, and include the name of the page. Do not send passwords or recovery codes.
